==Battleground==
*300 [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 3.33~20 seconds<sup>100f~600f</sup>.
*2 [[Master A.|Master As]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 13.33 seconds<sup>400f</sup>.
*3 [[The Face|Faces]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 26.67~40 seconds<sup>800f~1,200f</sup>.
*1 [[Dagshund]] spawns after 20 seconds<sup>600f</sup>.
*8 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 186.67 seconds<sup>5,600f</sup>, delay 0.67~3.33 seconds<sup>20f~100f</sup>.
*50 [[Doge Dark]]s spawn after 186.67 seconds<sup>5,600f</sup>, delay 6.67~13.33 seconds<sup>200f~400f</sup>.
*1 [[Bears Be Bare]] spawns as the boss after 186.67 seconds<sup>5,600f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**16 [[Those Guys]] spawn, delay 0.07~4 seconds<sup>2f~120f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Once the stage begins, upgrade your [[Worker Cat]] to level 4. If the Dagshund is at your base, start spamming all your meatshields and heavy attackers ([[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Bahamut Cat]] for example). Remember to keep spamming otherwise the Master A. will get through and kill your attackers. For The Face, you can use [[:Category:Anti-Floating Cats|anti-Floating]] cats to speed up the process, although it's not necessary as The Face's slow attack rate makes it so he shouldn't advance to your base.

